    "name": "CircleConnect Nexus",
    "description": "CircleConnect Nexus is a large-scale social networking platform designed around community \"circles\" where users collaborate on events, shared purchases, and crowdsourced goals. Built with a strict Model\u2013View\u2013Controller skeleton, the application separates domain logic (circles, posts, pledges, events), delivery (RESTful JSON + server-rendered pages), and presentation (responsive SPA widgets) to keep user-driven features\u2014such as real-time circle feeds, member voting, and pooled-payment pledges\u2014safe, testable, and independently evolvable.  \n\nThe project stresses the social dimension by weaving collective interactions into every major user story: circles can open micro-funding campaigns, members can co-edit event schedules, and influence scores steer content visibility. Core requirements include SSL-everywhere transport, OAuth2 social log-ins, stripe-backed pledge payments, granular activity logging, and an admin observability panel\u2014all orchestrated through Spring Boot MVC controllers, service components, repositories, and React/Thymeleaf hybrid views. With 52 target source files and ~335k tokens, the codebase offers a full spectrum of advanced social-app concerns: rate-limited REST endpoints, sophisticated validation layers, repository abstractions over PostgreSQL, adaptive UI, and an extensible middleware chain for authentication, session and error handling.",
